# reference.in: this family's reference requirements, resolved to the exact, hashed reference.lock
# beside this file by `python -m rcp_ndcg_test.jobs.reference_lock` (owner decision 35). The tool
# constrains torch and the CUDA stack to the engine image's freeze; every other pin installs into
# the family's reference venv and takes precedence over the image's copy. Never edit the lock by hand.
# The Qwen3-Reranker family's reference environment (one file for all three sizes, decision 34):
# what reference.py needs, in ITS OWN python (never the harness's process, never the engine image).
# transformers 4.57.6 is the paper-era pin; the reference runs on the image's torch (decision 35) and
# flash-attn is deliberately NOT pinned: the reference declares reference.attn_implementation: sdpa
# (GPU-E1: the stock reference environment has no compiled extras, and the follow-up measured sdpa
# references with Kendall tau 1.0 and max |delta| <= 0.041 on all three sizes). The reference's render
# mode (stage 1) needs only tokenizers + huggingface-hub; the score mode (stage 2, GPU) needs the rest.
#
# huggingface-hub ships with transformers; listed so a render-only install stays explicit.

torch>=2.0
transformers==4.57.6
accelerate>=1.10
huggingface-hub>=0.30,<1.0  # transformers 4.57.6 requires <1.0 (the image ships 1.33.0)
tokenizers>=0.21
